===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*seh₁p-|*-os|*-s}}
From {{inh|en|enm|savour|t=flavour; flavouring; taste; smell; appetite; characteristic; essence; attractiveness; delight, pleasure; knowledge, wisdom}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sāvǒur|pos=n|id=MED38653}}</ref> from {{der|en|xno|saveur}}, {{m|xno|savor}}, {{m|xno|savour}}, and {{der|en|fro|saveur}}, {{m|fro|savor}}, {{m|fro|savour|t=flavour; flavouring; taste; scent; delight, pleasure; knowledge, wisdom}} (modern {{cog|fr|saveur}}), from {{der|en|la|sapor|t=flavour; taste; scent; smell}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|entry=savour {{!}} savor|pos=n|id=5411002190|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> from {{m|la|sapiō|t=to taste of (something); to have a flavour}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sep-|*seh₁p-, *sep-|to taste; to try out}}) + {{m|la|-or|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming third-{{glossary|declension}} {{glossary|masculine}} {{glossary|abstract noun}}s}}. {{doublet|en|sapor}}.

