====Verb====
{{en-verb}} {{term-label|en|British spelling}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To possess a particular taste or smell, or a distinctive quality.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|V|i|passage=This '''savours''' not much of distraction.}}
#* {{RQ:Spectator|III|262|31 December 1711|passage=I have rejected everything that '''savours''' of party.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1750|author=w:Joseph Bellamy|title=True Religion Delineated
|passage=Begone, thou impudent wretch, to hell, thy proper place: thou art a despiser of my glorious majesty, and your frame of spirit '''savours''' of blasphemy.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[appreciate]], [[enjoy]] or [[relish]] something.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 August 26|author=Andrew Mourant|title=Reinforced against future flooding|journal=Rail|page=58|text=A journey along the Conwy Valley line is one to '''savour''' for aficionados of scenic railways.}}
#: {{ux|en|He closed his eyes so he could really '''savour''' his dessert.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To [[season]].
#* '''1974''', W. R. Barron, ''{{w|Sir Gawain and the Green Knight}}'' (modern translation)
#*: {{...}} divers sorts of fish; some baked in bread, some broiled on the coals, some seethed, some in gravy '''savoured''' with spices, and all with condiments so cunning that it caused him delight.

